      {
        "title": "NariQ: BF16-level Qwen3.8-27B in a 10 GB file",
        "link": "https://huggingface.co/nari-labs/Qwen3.8-27B-NariQ-GGUF",
        "description": "<p>We built NariQ: 3-bit-or-lower quantizations of Qwen3.8-27B that retain near-BF16 quality across agentic tasks, math, multilingual reasoning, and image understanding.<p>To our knowledge, this is the first 3-bit-or-lower quantization that retains BF16 lvl performance on long-horizon agentic tasks.<p>Benchmarks (BF16 / 3-bit / 2.5-bit / 2-bit):<p>- DeepSWE: 39.8 / 41.0 / 41.9 / 28.6<p>- Terminal-Bench 2.1: 62.6 / 63.8 / 60.2 / 52.4<p>- AIME 25+26: 97.7 / 98.3 / 96.5 / 86.0<p>- MSGM: 94.0 / 93.1 / 91.8 / 90.6<p>- RealWorldQA: 82.4 / 82.4 / 81.3 / 80.9<p>Decode speed is comparable to other quants on an RTX PRO 6000. Context-length results below<p>(3-bit / 2.5-bit / 2-bit / Unsloth UD-IQ3_XXS):<p>- 4K: 88.9 / 99.2 / 111.7 / 94.7<p>- 16K: 84.5 / 93.8 / 105.1 / 89.8<p>- 64K: 70.7 / 77.5 / 85.0 / 74.8<p>Running these currently require our llama.cpp fork:\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/nari-labs/nari-llama.cpp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/nari-labs/nari-llama.cpp</a>)<p>Feedback and questions welcome. We'd love to hear how these perform on your workloads.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50611402\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50611402</a></p>\n<p>Points: 169</p>\n<p># Comments: 34</p>",
        "pubDate": "Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:42:38 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50611402"
      }
